@node emacsvox-aural-planner
@section emacsvox-aural-planner

Infer presentation objects and formatting runs from captured source text,
resolve semantic policy once at the source boundary, and attach frozen
concrete plans.  This module performs no queueing or backend process work.

@node emacsvox-aural-preview
@section emacsvox-aural-preview

Coordinate explicit previews without owning their feature-specific content.
Speech previews stop earlier output, queue one concrete plan or caller-built
sequence, and dispatch once.  Cue-only previews stop speech but bypass the
speech queue, presentation history, and training hooks.

@subsection emacsvox-aural-preview Options

@defvar {User Option} emacsvox-aural-preview-label-verbosity
@verbatim
How physical voice comparisons identify their samples.
‘names’ includes the engine and voice; ‘brief’ uses only the comparison
letter or sequence number; nil omits labels.  The comparison sentence itself
is identical for every sample.
@end verbatim

Default Value:
@verbatim

names

@end verbatim

@end defvar

